---
import GuideArticleLayout from '../../layouts/GuideArticleLayout.astro';
---

<GuideArticleLayout 
	title="Display Styles, Sizes & Full Mode" 
	description="Learn about visual styling, resizing the timer, and utilizing focused Full mode."
>
	<section class="space-y-4">
		<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem] font-semibold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight">Display Styles</h2>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			You can switch between three visual styles for Timer, Clock, and Stopwatch from the top right Settings menu:
		</p>

		<dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5 my-4">
			<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
				<dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Modern</dt>
				<dd class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Clean, large numeric typography designed for immediate, prominent legibility.</dd>
			</div>
			<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
				<dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Digital</dt>
				<dd class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Retro seven-segment inspired layout providing a classic digital clock face.</dd>
			</div>
			<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
				<dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Analog</dt>
				<dd class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Traditional circular dial with sweeping hands. Shows an AM/PM badge in 12-hour Clock mode.</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>

		<p class="text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
			Changing the display style modifies only how the time is shown; it never resets or interrupts your active session.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-4">
		<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem] font-semibold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight">Display Sizes</h2>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			Scale the timer workspace to match your setup or focus environment by selecting a size option near the bottom right:
		</p>

		<dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3.5 my-4">
			<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
				<dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Tiny</dt>
				<dd class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Compact footprint when keeping the timer alongside other windows.</dd>
			</div>
			<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
				<dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Mid <span class="text-xs font-normal text-zinc-400 dark:text-zinc-500">(Default)</span></dt>
				<dd class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Standard balanced view for normal desk and laptop working distances.</dd>
			</div>
			<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
				<dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Big</dt>
				<dd class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">Expanded scale that remains easily readable from across the room.</dd>
			</div>
			<div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-50/70 dark:bg-zinc-900/50">
				<dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-1">Full</dt>
				<dd class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">App-level focused view hiding header, footer, and side panels. Exit with Esc or size toggle.</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>
	</section>

	<section class="space-y-4">
		<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-[1.65rem] font-semibold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight">Understanding Full Mode</h2>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			Full mode is an in-app focused layout designed to eliminate visual distractions like the navigation bar and footer. Essential timer controls remain accessible on screen.
		</p>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			<strong class="font-medium text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">Note:</strong> Full mode is a layout setting within On Screen Timer. It is <em>not</em> the browser's native Fullscreen API (F11 on most platforms). You can combine both for the most distraction-free experience.
		</p>
		<p class="text-base sm:text-[16px] text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
			To exit Full mode, simply press <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200 bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 border border-zinc-300 dark:border-zinc-700 rounded">Esc</kbd> on your keyboard or select a different size from the display options.
		</p>
	</section>
</GuideArticleLayout>
